BEGIN;

UPDATE grammar_chapters SET
  title = 'Prepositions & Dependency Rules',
  position = 4,
  estimated_min = 30,
  difficulty = 2,
  band_target = 'Band 6 accuracy',
  summary = 'Fix the preposition pairs and dependent prepositions that leak marks in Task 1 trends and Task 2 argumentation.',
  content = $content${"version": 1, "blocks": [{"id": "b01", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Prepositions are the small words (in, on, at, by, for, to, of, from, with) that show how other words relate in time, place, and direction. They look trivial, but they carry a large share of the errors on this test, for one reason: prepositions are memorised by pattern, not by logic. There is no rule that explains why English says interested in but good at and afraid of. These are fixed collocations."}, {"id": "b02", "type": "paragraph", "text": "For a Bangla speaker, that is a problem, because your instinct is to translate the Bangla preposition directly, and Bangla maps its relationships differently. This chapter gives you the high-frequency patterns to memorise as blocks, and it targets the specific direct-translation errors that mark a script as Bangladeshi."}, {"id": "b03", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "4.1 What a preposition does"}, {"id": "b04", "type": "paragraph", "text": "A preposition sits before a noun or pronoun and shows a relationship: the book is on the table (place), the meeting is at three (time), she walked into the room (direction). One key rule: after a preposition, a verb always takes the -ing form, never the infinitive -- interested in studying, responsible for managing, capable of solving."}, {"id": "b05", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "4.2 Prepositions of time -- in, on, at"}, {"id": "b06", "type": "table", "headers": ["Preposition", "Used with", "Examples"], "rows": [["in", "months, years, seasons, centuries, long periods", "in July, in 2020, in winter, in the 1990s"], ["on", "days and dates", "on Monday, on 5 May, on weekdays"], ["at", "clock times and fixed points", "at 5 p.m., at night, at the weekend, at the start"]]}, {"id": "b07", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Other time prepositions that matter: since + a starting point that reaches now (since 2010); for + a duration (for ten years); during + a named period (during the war); by + a deadline (by 2030); between X and Y for a span (between 2000 and 2010)."}, {"id": "b08", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "4.3 Task 1 data prepositions"}, {"id": "b09", "type": "table", "headers": ["Phrase", "Use", "Example"], "rows": [["increase / rise by", "the size of a change", "rose by 10 per cent"], ["from X to Y", "start and end points", "grew from 10 to 20 million"], ["a rise / an increase of", "after the noun form", "an increase of 10 per cent"], ["reach a peak / stand at", "a specific value", "peaked at 40 per cent"], ["fall / drop to", "the destination value", "fell to a low of 5"], ["between X and Y", "a range or a time span", "between 2000 and 2010"]]}, {"id": "b10", "type": "example_pair", "incorrect": "Sales increased with 20 per cent and reached to a peak in June.", "correct": "Sales increased by 20 per cent and reached a peak in June.", "why": "increase by a percentage; reach a peak takes no preposition after reach."}, {"id": "b11", "type": "heading", "level": 2, "text": "4.4 Dependent prepositions (verb / adjective / noun)"}, {"id": "b12", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Many verbs, adjectives, and nouns are followed by a fixed preposition. There is no logic; learn each as a unit."}, {"id": "b13", "type": "table", "headers": ["Collocation", "Example"], "rows": [["depend on", "The outcome depends on funding."], ["lead to", "Industrialisation leads to pollution."], ["result in / result from", "The policy resulted in higher costs. / The damage resulted from neglect."], ["contribute to", "Cars contribute to air pollution."], ["consist of", "The panel consists of five experts."], ["deal with / cope with", "Governments must deal with poverty."], ["focus on / concentrate on", "The essay focuses on two causes."], ["rely on / benefit from", "Rural areas rely on agriculture. / Students benefit from feedback."], ["suffer from", "Many cities suffer from congestion."], ["invest in / participate in / apply for", "Governments should invest in transport."], ["interested in / good at / afraid of", "She is interested in studying abroad."], ["responsible for / related to", "He is responsible for managing the team."], ["solution to / increase in / lack of", "Education is the solution to many problems."]]}, {"id": "b14", "type": "l1_error_fixer", "title": "Direct-translation preposition errors", "body": "These errors come from translating Bangla patterns word-for-word. Memorise the correct English form as a block.", "error_types": [{"label": "discuss about / mention about / investigate about", "incorrect": "We discussed about the policy. / She mentioned about three solutions.", "correct": "We discussed the policy. / She mentioned three solutions."}, {"label": "according to me / emphasise on / return back", "incorrect": "According to me, the government should act. / He emphasised on grammar. / They returned back home.", "correct": "In my opinion, the government should act. / He emphasised grammar. / They returned home."}, {"label": "enter into / marry with / comprise of / cope up with", "incorrect": "He entered into the room. / She married with a doctor. / The report comprises of five sections.", "correct": "He entered the room. / She married a doctor. / The report comprises five sections / is composed of five sections."}]}, {"id": "b15", "type": "ielts_impact", "skills": ["writing", "speaking"], "title": "Small words, real marks", "body": "Prepositions affect your score in two visible places. In Writing Task 1, the data prepositions (by, from, to, of, at) are so standard that getting one wrong stands out immediately. In Task 2 and Speaking, dependent prepositions and direct-translation errors separate controlled from uncontrolled English. Because these are collocations, correct ones also lift Lexical Resource.", "examples": {"task1": "Unemployment rose by four points, from six to ten per cent, before falling to eight in 2015.", "task2": "A lack of investment in public transport contributes to congestion and leads to higher emissions.", "speaking": "It really depends on the situation, but on balance I think education is the solution to most of these problems."}}]}$content$::jsonb,
  is_published = true,
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'ch4-prepositions';

INSERT INTO grammar_exercises (id, chapter_id, slug, title, kind, instructions, items, position, is_published)
VALUES (
  'a1000001-0001-4000-8000-000000000241',
  'a1000001-0001-4000-8000-000000000104',
  'ex-4-1-preposition-fill',
  'Exercise 4.1 - Preposition Fill-in',
  'correction',
  'Fill each gap with the correct preposition. Some gaps take no preposition; write (0) for those.',
  $items1$[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "The number of tourists rose ______ 20 per cent last year.", "answer": "by", "accepted": ["by"], "reason": "Size of change uses by.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "The figure grew ______ 5 million ______ 8 million ______ 2015.", "answer": "from / to / in", "accepted": ["from to in", "from, to, in"], "reason": "from X to Y for endpoints; in + year.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "Air pollution largely results ______ vehicle emissions.", "answer": "from", "accepted": ["from"], "reason": "result from = cause.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "The government should invest more ______ renewable energy.", "answer": "in", "accepted": ["in"], "reason": "invest in.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "She is very interested ______ studying abroad.", "answer": "in", "accepted": ["in"], "reason": "interested in + -ing.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Rapid urbanisation has led ______ a housing shortage.", "answer": "to", "accepted": ["to"], "reason": "lead to.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q7", "prompt": "Unemployment peaked ______ 12 per cent ______ 2009.", "answer": "at / in", "accepted": ["at in", "at, in"], "reason": "peak at a value; in + year.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q8", "prompt": "The success of the plan depends ______ adequate funding.", "answer": "on", "accepted": ["on"], "reason": "depend on.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q9", "prompt": "Many students suffer ______ a lack ______ confidence.", "answer": "from / of", "accepted": ["from of", "from, of"], "reason": "suffer from; a lack of.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q10", "prompt": "He is responsible ______ managing the entire department.", "answer": "for", "accepted": ["for"], "reason": "responsible for + -ing.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q11", "prompt": "This problem is closely related ______ poverty.", "answer": "to", "accepted": ["to"], "reason": "related to.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q12", "prompt": "We must discuss ______ the main causes of the issue.", "answer": "(0)", "accepted": ["(0)", "0", "no preposition", ""], "reason": "discuss takes a direct object -- no about.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q13", "prompt": "There has been a sharp increase ______ demand ______ housing.", "answer": "in / for", "accepted": ["in for", "in, for"], "reason": "increase in; demand for.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q14", "prompt": "The committee consists ______ seven members.", "answer": "of", "accepted": ["of"], "reason": "consist of.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q15", "prompt": "The shop is closed ______ Fridays but open ______ the weekend.", "answer": "on / at", "accepted": ["on at", "on, at"], "reason": "on + day; at the weekend (BrE).", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q16", "prompt": "Consumption fell ______ a low ______ five units in 2012.", "answer": "to / of", "accepted": ["to of", "to, of"], "reason": "fall to; a low of.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q17", "prompt": "Cities in the region rely heavily ______ agriculture.", "answer": "on", "accepted": ["on"], "reason": "rely on.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q18", "prompt": "The report focuses ______ the effects ______ climate change.", "answer": "on / of", "accepted": ["on of", "on, of"], "reason": "focus on; effects of.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q19", "prompt": "Please enter ______ the hall quietly.", "answer": "(0)", "accepted": ["(0)", "0", "no preposition", ""], "reason": "enter takes a direct object -- no into needed here.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q20", "prompt": "The two graphs are similar ______ each other.", "answer": "to", "accepted": ["to"], "reason": "similar to.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q21", "prompt": "Students benefit greatly ______ regular feedback.", "answer": "from", "accepted": ["from"], "reason": "benefit from.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q22", "prompt": "She applied ______ a scholarship ______ a British university.", "answer": "for / to", "accepted": ["for to", "for, to"], "reason": "apply for something; apply to an institution.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q23", "prompt": "A good education is the solution ______ many social problems.", "answer": "to", "accepted": ["to"], "reason": "solution to.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q24", "prompt": "The population has been rising steadily ______ 2000.", "answer": "since", "accepted": ["since"], "reason": "since + starting point reaching now.", "bn_note": null}, {"id": "q25", "prompt": "According ______ the chart, spending increased sharply.", "answer": "to", "accepted": ["to"], "reason": "according to (source), not according to me.", "bn_note": null}]$items1$::jsonb,
  1,
  true
)
